_money.py expects banker's rounding, but src/money.py used ROUND_HALF_UP.\n\nChanges:\n- src/money.py: switch `round_money` from ROUND_HALF_UP to ROUND_HALF_EVEN, matching its docstring and FIN-212.\n\nVerification:\n- Branch was updated with latest main (merge commit 0a9452f727) after the PR was rejected as behind main.\n- CI run ci-0002 on commit 0a9452f727: passed.\n- Expected values: 2.675 -> 2.68 and 2.665 -> 2.66 under half-even.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-0a9452f727"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in a pull request, PR #101, with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Root cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. The test expects 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66, which is half-even behavior.\n- **Change:** switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`.\n- **CI:** the first run (`ci-0001`, commit 08d3cd5986) passed. The PR was then rejected because the branch was behind main, so I merged main into the branch (commit 0a9452f727) and re-ran CI (`ci-0002`), which also passed. The PR was opened against that commit.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so alex or another code owner still needs to approve it.", "type": "text"}]}]}